  "question": {
    "text": "A given object takes $n$ times more time to slide down a $45^{\\circ}$ rough inclined plane as it takes to slide down a perfectly smooth $45^{\\circ}$ incline. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the object and the incline is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1CPMD",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{n^2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9jAgi",
      "text": "\n$1-\\frac{1}{n^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "FBzpC",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2-n^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4tY2y",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-n^2}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The coefficients of kinetic friction between the object and the incline\n$\\mu=\\tan \\theta\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2}\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mu=1-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2} \\quad\\left(\\because \\theta=45^{\\circ}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
